    analysis: 'The ingress attachment selects the VRF before the destination lookup. RD-qualified VPN NLRI preserves otherwise identical prefixes. RTs determine eligible import. The service label identifies egress disposition, while the outer transport gets the packet to its owner. Per-prefix, per-CE and per-VRF label modes change label scale and egress lookup behavior, subject to hardware support.',
    proposal: 'Keep unique per-PE/VRF RDs, explicit per-family RT membership and exact PE/CE host allowlists. Select a qualified label mode against measured label/FIB resources and service needs. Use the ACME-only marker experiment to corroborate separation beyond overlapping positive probes.',
    implementation: 'Create both VRFs and families, bind each attachment with its documented addresses, establish scoped CE routing, then enable PE–RR VPNv4/v6. Verify each pipeline stage before running customer traffic. Record actual service-label allocation mode and transport recursion.',
